  "evidenceBoundary": {
    "exact": "Selected native identities, ordinary primitive ABI records, source getter/vector declarations and complete selected unwind families with individually hashed, fully partitioned code ranges and owned sparse control-flow joins.",
    "direct": "Same selected MissionCondition record supplies State and IsSame. Literal IsSame==1 chooses equality to the same-ordinal provider Int32 return; every other Int32 chooses inequality. Anonymous cache byte update returns a changed flag. On the selected nonnull query route, the opaque lookup object supplies an Int32 key to the explicitly bound Dictionary<Int32,Int32>.TryGetValue request. A true result returns its Int32 output; a false result returns zero.",
    "conditional": "Selected non-replacement update, query and generated State/IsSame paths, valid cache/grid pointers and normal callee returns. Nonzero vector slot and a valid selected record are required for stored-record semantics; the absent-vector path is authenticated as a zero carrier, without claiming its getter reads are valid. Int32 index shifting and position addition must not wrap. Win64 nonvolatile-register preservation, normal stack isolation and stable source storage are required. Direct fixed-frame stores on admitted paths do not overlap the saved provider Int32 local; indirect stores and called bodies are not a global memory-isolation proof.",
    "unresolved": "Id/IsQuest target meaning, provider value origin, authored Conditions-to-live cache join, aggregation byte source, hotSlot-to-file/grid ownership, runtime invocation and condition truth remain unresolved."
  },
